  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between Psammaplin D and the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex, mediated through Fucosyltransferase 9. This is supported by three distinct pathways, all of which indicate that Psammaplin D targets Fucosyltransferase 9, which in turn is a target of multiple compounds, including Semiplenamide A and (2R,4R)-16-Heptadecyne-1,2,4-triol. These compounds all ultimately interact with the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex, suggesting a common downstream pathway. The high scores (final_score=0.691) across these paths indicate a strong, consistent relationship, likely due to the shared biological role of Fucosyltransferase 9 in the regulation of the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex. The evidence suggests that Psammaplin D may act as a modulator of this pathway, potentially influencing the activity of the complex. However, the exact mechanism by which Psammaplin D affects Fucosyltransferase 9 or its downstream targets remains to be elucidated, and further experimental validation is needed to confirm the direct interaction between Psammaplin D and the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex.",
